# Trace AI Hero MDX rendering and the crash course

## Step

Establish how lesson body content becomes rendered React in AI Hero, what custom
MDX components already exist, and what "the crash course" concretely is. This is
the step that decides how hard wiring a `<Quiz>` MDX component actually is.

Read (do not modify) in `~/Code/badass-courses/ai-hero/apps/ai-hero`, plus
`~/Code/badass-courses/course-builder/packages/**` where AI Hero imports from it.

Answer these, each with file:line evidence:

1. **The MDX pipeline.** How does a lesson's body string become rendered output?
   Name the library (next-mdx-remote, MDXRemote, mdx-bundler, compiled at build
   time, compiled at request time — find out which), where compilation happens
   (server component, RSC, client), and every place a component map is passed in.
2. **The component map.** Enumerate the custom components already available to
   authors inside a lesson body. For each, show how it is registered and give a
   usage example from real content if one exists. This is the list a `<Quiz>`
   would join.
3. Can a component in that map be a **client component with state**? Show an
   existing example that holds state or does data fetching, or prove none exists.
   Say what constrains this (RSC boundaries, serialization of props, etc.).
4. Can a component in that map receive a **structured object prop** —
   i.e. does `<QuizQuestion data={{...}} />` with a real JS object literal work
   in this pipeline, or does MDX-in-database force props to be strings? Test the
   claim against the actual compile path. This is decisive for Matt's requested
   shape.
5. **The crash course.** Find what Matt means. Look for a product, course, or
   content resource in AI Hero that is called a crash course or is clearly the
   current free intro offering. Identify its content resources, where its lesson
   bodies live, and how Matt authors them today (admin UI? repo files? the
   course-sync path in `packages/course-sync-schema`?).
6. **How Matt authors content today.** Trace the actual write path an author or
   an author's agent uses to change a lesson body. If `course-sync` is that path,
   describe its schema and what fields it can carry — specifically whether it
   could carry quiz data.
7. What existing components, if any, already do something quiz-like or
   interactive inside lesson bodies?

## Deliverable

Write your findings into this file as a `## Result (2026-07-24)` section.
Lead with the MDX pipeline narrative, then a table of available MDX components,
then the answers to the numbered questions, with question 4 called out plainly
as YES or NO with evidence. Set `status: "closed"` and add
`closed_at: "2026-07-24"` to the frontmatter. Cite `path:line` for every claim.
No product recommendations — facts only.

## Result (2026-07-24)

### Pipeline narrative

A workshop lesson is a `lesson` content resource whose `fields.body` is a string
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/lessons.ts:12-31`). The workshop lesson server component
checks access, then passes that string to AI Hero's `compileMDX` with an empty
call-site component map and the lesson id
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/(content)/workshops/[module]/[lesson]/(view)/shared-page.tsx:34-70`).
`compileMDX` uses `compileMDX` from `next-mdx-remote/rsc`, sanitizes only HTML
comments, and compiles the body at request/render time on the server
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:23-29`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/sanitize-mdx-source.ts:1-3`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:259-296`). The returned React-node promise
crosses into the client `LessonBody`, which unwraps it with React `use()` and
renders `content` (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/(content)/workshops/_components/lesson-body.tsx:1-20`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/(content)/workshops/_components/lesson-body.tsx:47-56`).

The lesson call site passes `{}` as its component map
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/(content)/workshops/[module]/[lesson]/(view)/shared-page.tsx:65-70`).
`compileMDXInternal` passes one merged map to `next-mdx-remote/rsc`: first the
shared Course Builder map, then AI Hero's map, then call-site overrides
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:285-300`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:314-488`). If full MDX compilation fails,
the fallback passes an empty map and escapes MDX-significant tokens
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:183-205`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:525-551`).

