The map also overrides markdown/HTML elements: lesson checkboxes become
persistent `MDXCheckbox` instances when a lesson id exists; `h1`-`h3`, `a`,
`img`, `input`, and `hr` have custom renderers
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:301-313`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:350-354`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:419-447`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:386-388`).

### Numbered answers

#### 1. The MDX pipeline

This is `next-mdx-remote` v6's RSC compiler, not `MDXRemote`, `mdx-bundler`, or a
build-time import (`apps/ai-hero/package.json:194`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:26-29`). Compilation starts in the lesson
server component after access succeeds, at request/render time
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/(content)/workshops/[module]/[lesson]/(view)/shared-page.tsx:51-70`).
The map handoffs are: lesson call-site `{}` at `shared-page.tsx:65-70`; wrapper
arguments/defaults at `compile-mdx.tsx:566-587`; merged runtime map at
`compile-mdx.tsx:285-300,314-488`; and empty-map degraded fallback at
`compile-mdx.tsx:188-205`.

#### 2. The component map

The table above enumerates the lesson runtime map. The shared factory provides
all `COMMON_MDX` and `PAGE_MDX` implementations and AI Hero spreads it first so
local entries win
(`/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/course-builder/packages/ui/cms/mdx-components/index.tsx:246-257,383-400`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:285-300`). Repo-tracked content contains a
real `ThemeImage` object-prop example and a `Testimonial` example, but no
repo-tracked workshop lesson bodies; those bodies live in content resources or
the external course manifest (`apps/ai-hero/content/cohort-copy.mdx:17`,
`apps/ai-hero/content/landing.md:48-52`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/lessons.ts:12-31`).

#### 3. Client components with state

**YES.** The runtime map dynamically loads client components
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:40-98`). `Spoiler` is a concrete mapped
example with `useState` and a reveal button
(`/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/course-builder/packages/ui/cms/mdx-components/interactive.tsx:1-13,25-64`).
`Commit` is another mapped client component with open/copy state
(`apps/ai-hero/src/components/mdx/commit-map.tsx:1-4,52-70`). Lesson markdown
checkboxes are converted to `MDXCheckbox`, which stores state in IndexedDB
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:301-313`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/components/mdx-checkbox.tsx:1-46`). The server compiler emits
an RSC tree containing those client boundaries; props crossing a client boundary
must therefore be serializable. The existing mapped client examples receive
strings, booleans, and React children, not functions
(`apps/ai-hero/src/components/mdx-checkbox.tsx:14-22`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/components/mdx/commit-map.tsx:52-58`).

#### 4. Structured object props

**YES.** A lesson body can use `<QuizQuestion data={{ ... }} />` with a real,
plain structured object after that component name is registered. The actual
compile call uses `next-mdx-remote/rsc` with `blockJS: false`, so MDX expressions
are compiled rather than reduced to strings
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:285-296,489-515`). The sanitizer removes
only HTML comments and does not rewrite braces
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/sanitize-mdx-source.ts:1-3`). The repository already
contains the same syntax in real MDX:
`<ThemeImage urls={{ dark: "...", light: "..." }} ... />`
(`apps/ai-hero/content/cohort-copy.mdx:17`), and the registered renderer receives
`urls` as `{ dark: string; light: string }`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:345-349`). The editor's shared snippet
also emits this exact object-literal syntax
(`/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/course-builder/packages/ui/cms/manifests/page.ts:64-71`).
A plain data object is serializable across the RSC/client boundary; a function in
that object would not meet the client-boundary shape demonstrated by the mapped
client components (`apps/ai-hero/src/components/mdx-checkbox.tsx:14-22`).

#### 5. The crash course

The concrete resource is the draft **AI Coding Crash Course**. Its active binding
is named `csb_ai_coding_crash_course`, points at source course
`50385098-a712-486f-b777-1f76ef31e9e5`, product `product-ma254`, and anchor
workshop `workshop-2ozd9`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/types.ts:7-16`). The sync system's own edit URL is
`https://www.aihero.dev/workshops/ai-coding-crash-course/edit`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/detection-poller.ts:9-11`). Its sections become
children of that anchor workshop, and each lesson becomes a lesson content
resource whose body is the primary video's `body` string
(`apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/control-plane.ts:175-236`). Applying a run writes
those fields into `contentResource` and version rows
(`apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/drizzle-persistence.ts:400-425,470-532`).

The separate public named course **AI SDK v6 Crash Course** is present at
`/workshops/ai-sdk-v6-crash-course`; the old v5 route redirects to it
(`apps/ai-hero/src/components/navigation/use-nav-links.tsx:94-103`,
`apps/ai-hero/next.config.mjs:78-83`). The draft sync binding and explicit
`ai-coding-crash-course/edit` URL are the source-code resource that matches the
new Course Video Manager authoring flow; no source file identifies the public
AI SDK v6 slug with that binding.

#### 6. How Matt authors content today

The crash-course source path is Course Video Manager -> Dropbox ->
`/course.json` -> AI Hero's draft course-sync control plane. The scheduled
Inngest function polls every 30 minutes and reads the Dropbox manifest
(`apps/ai-hero/src/inngest/functions/course-sync-detection-poller.ts:22-33`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/inngest/functions/course-sync-detection-poller.ts:34-55`). The
Dropbox reader fetches `/course.json`, requires schema v3, and identifies the
producer as `course-video-manager`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/dropbox-course-sync.ts:380-431`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/dropbox-course-sync.ts:451-476`). The API also exposes
binding lookup plus authenticated stage, preview, apply, read, and rollback
operations (`apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/generated-client.ts:39-88`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/openapi.ts:28-111`).

The v3 manifest carries course/version/name, sections, lesson ids/titles/types,
and video records with `body`, `description`, media hashes/paths/bytes, and
chapters (`packages/course-sync-schema/src/course-json-v3.ts:23-78`). It has no
quiz-specific field, and decoding rejects excess properties
(`packages/course-sync-schema/src/course-json-v3.ts:86-89`). It **can carry quiz
markup inside the existing `body` string**, because sync copies that string
verbatim to lesson `fields.body`; it cannot carry separate typed quiz data under
its current exact schema (`apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/control-plane.ts:225-236`).

A direct admin write path also exists. The lesson edit route loads the lesson and
renders `EditLessonClient`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/(content)/workshops/[module]/[lesson]/edit/page.tsx:42-93`).
That client builds the shared lesson editor
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/(content)/workshops/[module]/[lesson]/edit/edit-lesson-client.tsx:65-119`),
whose manifest declares `fields.body` and the `COMMON_MDX` picker
(`/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/course-builder/packages/ui/cms/manifests/lesson.ts:120-132`).
The body surface is a raw MDX textarea with slash/snippet insertion
(`/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/course-builder/packages/ui/cms/body-editor.tsx:325-375,527-550`),
and save passes the body string to `updateLesson`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/cms/lesson-bindings.ts:70-107`), which merges and writes
resource fields (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/lessons-query.ts:453-511`).

#### 7. Existing quiz-like lesson components

No `Quiz`, `QuizQuestion`, correctness, answer-key, or grading component exists
in the lesson runtime map (`apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx:285-488`). The
closest interactive lesson-body pieces are: persistent IndexedDB checkboxes
(`apps/ai-hero/src/components/mdx-checkbox.tsx:8-46`), `Spoiler` reveal state
(`/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/course-builder/packages/ui/cms/mdx-components/interactive.tsx:25-64`),
and copy-command interactions in `Commit`/`Recommendation`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/components/mdx/commit-map.tsx:52-70`,
`/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/course-builder/packages/ui/cms/mdx-components/interactive.tsx:111-174`).
None of those records a selected answer or compares it with a correct answer.
